# Security Guardrails (Non-Negotiable)

- Never weaken or remove authentication, RBAC, IDOR checks, CSRF checks, rate limits, CORS allowlist, or security headers.
- Any new mutating backend endpoint (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`) must require authenticated user + CSRF validation.
- Any new resource-by-ID endpoint must verify ownership or admin access before returning/changing data.
- Keep Pydantic request schemas strict (`extra="forbid"`), and avoid raw SQL string execution.
- Never add `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or unsanitized user-content rendering on frontend.
- Keep token/session cookies `HttpOnly` and `Secure` in production; use `SameSite=None` with `Secure` for cross-origin SPA→API hosts (e.g. Vercel + Render). Prefer `lax`/`strict` only when frontend and API are same-site.
- Never hardcode secrets, credentials, or private connection strings; use environment variables only.
- Any security-sensitive change must keep `backend/scripts/security_lint.py`, dependency audits, and CI security gates passing.
